  "description": "IXONIT crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C50 H50 N14 O20 Tb4,4(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.779-4.040 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.85-118.74°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C54H66N14O26Tb4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
